{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:AppendixStandardModel.SmHyperchargeInvariant","@type":"LeanModule","name":"AppendixStandardModel.SmHyperchargeInvariant","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Groupoid","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.HyperchargeInvariant.exists_writhe_degenerate_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.HyperchargeInvariant.exists_writhe_degenerate_pair","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-hypercharge-invariant.lean#L82-L93","doc":"Any hypercharge invariant forces a writhe-degenerate pair: two\nstates with equal writhe but distinct hypercharge (the proton–neutron\nconfiguration). Proved from the factorization criterion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.HyperchargeInvariant.exists_hypercharge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.HyperchargeInvariant.exists_hypercharge","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-hypercharge-invariant.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Existence of gauge-invariant `I₃` and `Y` with Gell-Mann–Nishijima\nholding and `Y` not a function of the writhe. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.HyperchargeInvariant.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.HyperchargeInvariant.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-hypercharge-invariant.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.HyperchargeInvariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.HyperchargeInvariant","kind":"class","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-hypercharge-invariant.lean#L57-L80","doc":"**Conjecture (hypercharge invariant).** Over a groupoid `S` of\ntopological states with a charge function `Q` and a writhe function\n`w`, there exist isospin and hypercharge functions `I₃, Y` that are\nconstant on gauge orbits, satisfy the Gell-Mann–Nishijima relation\n`Q = I₃ + Y/2`, and — the sharp clause — `Y` does **not** factor\nthrough the writhe. By `factors_through_iff`, the last clause is\nequivalent to the existence of a writhe-degenerate pair of states\nseparated by `Y`; physically, the missing second invariant must\nseparate states the writhe cannot.\n\nIntended instantiation: `S` = knot-state groupoid, `Q` the Coulomb\ncharge `w/2` reading at the hadron level, `w` the writhe. Open: no\ncandidate invariant currently passes; the ribbon-framing twist is a\nrecorded candidate direction, untested. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:sm-hypercharge-invariant","label":"conj:sm-hypercharge-invariant","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-hypercharge-invariant.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.StandardModel.factors_through_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.StandardModel.factors_through_iff","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-standard-model/sm-hypercharge-invariant.lean#L39-L55","doc":"**Factorization criterion** (proved). A function `Y` factors\nthrough `w` iff `Y` is constant on the fibres of `w`. The reverse\ndirection builds the factoring map by choice on nonempty fibres. ","signatureChunk":0}]}